{
  "summary": "Refactors block and header processing functions in `validation.cpp` to return `BlockValidationState` by value instead of returning a boolean and populating a `BlockValidationState&` out-parameter. Adds static factory helpers `MakeInvalid` and `MakeError` to `BlockValidationState` for concise inline state construction. Callers across `net_processing`, the kernel C API, node storage, RPC, benchmarks, and unit tests are adjusted to match the new signatures.",
  "problem": "Validation functions used a dual-reporting pattern with a boolean return code alongside an out-parameter `BlockValidationState`. This allows return values and state objects to diverge, obscures whether an input state is read or overwritten, and risks state pollution across sequential calls where a pre-existing invalid state prevents subsequent failure details from being recorded.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes the change grew out of review feedback on kernel PR #33856 to eliminate ambiguity in process_block_header return semantics.",
    "Eliminates redundant error returns in the kernel C API (`btck_chainstate_manager_process_block_header`) where returning both an integer code and an out-parameter created ambiguity."
  ],
