  "scope_notes": "Mechanical refactor of calling conventions across 12 commits ordered bottom-to-top through the validation call hierarchy, touching block validation entry points and test harnesses.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased with minor commit refinements and added co-authorship on the `FatalError`, `ProcessNewBlockHeaders`, and `AcceptBlock` commits.",
  "card": "This PR refactors block validation functions including CheckBlock, AcceptBlock, FlushStateToDisk, and ProcessNewBlockHeaders to return BlockValidationState by value instead of using an out-parameter and a boolean return. It resolves potential inconsistencies between the boolean status and the validation state object, while preventing state pollution across chained calls. The change was motivated by kernel interface cleanups discussed in PR 33856 and has no open dependencies.",
